'''''Loropetalum''''' is a genus of four species of [[shrub]]s or small trees in the [[witch-hazel]] family, [[Hamamelidaceae]], native to [[China]], [[Japan]], and south-eastern [[Asia]].{{sfn|Zhang et al|2004}}

==Description==
[[Flower]]s are produced in clusters during spring and are similar to those of the closely related [[witch-hazel]]. Each flower consists of four to six (depending on species) slender strap shaped petals 1–2&nbsp;cm long.

==Taxonomy==
''Loropetalum'' is placed in tribe Loropetaleae, subfamily Hamamelidoideae, family [[Hamamelidaceae]] of the [[Saxifragales]].{{sfn|Averyanov et al|2018}}{{sfn|Li|Bogle|2001}}

===Etymology===
The name ''Loropetalum'' refers to the shape of the flowers and comes from the Greek ''loron'' meaning strap and ''petalon'' meaning petal.

===Species===
The species are:
*''[[Loropetalum chinense]]'' – white-flowering variety up to {{Convert abbreviated|3.7|m}} tall, pink-flowering variety up to {{Convert abbreviated|1.5|m}} tall
*''[[Loropetalum flavum]]'' – yellow flowers
*''[[Loropetalum lanceum]]'' – up to {{Convert abbreviated|13|m}} tall, white flowers
*''[[Loropetalum subcordatum]]'' – up to {{Convert abbreviated|12|m}} tall

